  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "x": 80.0,
      "y": -38.0,
      "text": "Gains from lqr(A, B, Q, R) with A = [0 1; 0 -2], B = [0; 2], Q = diag(100, 0), R = 1: K =\n[10, 2.317]. KR = K1 gives zero steady-state error. For a real motor, wire an encoder\ncount and a speed estimate to X1 and X2."
